TCC(1)                         User Commands                         TCC(1)

NAME
    tcc - Tiny C Compiler

SYNOPSIS
    tcc [options] file...
    tcc -v

DESCRIPTION
    TCC is a small, fast C compiler. On Horus it is the unmodified upstream
    TinyCC 0.9.27 (x86-64 target), ported to run as a ring-3 program from
    /bin/tcc over the fs_server. Its assembler and linker are built in, so it
    needs no external toolchain: TCC alone turns C into an object or an
    executable.

    TCC emits x86-64 ELF, the same format Horus's own loader consumes.

OPTIONS
    -v             show the version; -vv is more verbose
    -c             compile only, producing an object file (.o), no link
    -o outfile     write output to outfile
    -Idir          add dir to the #include search path
    -Dsym[=val]    define a preprocessor macro
    -Uym           undefine a preprocessor macro
    -Ldir          add dir to the library search path
    -llib          link against liblib
    -g             generate debug information
    -w             suppress warnings

    Run `tcc -h` for the full option list.

HORUS NOTES
    This build targets x86-64 only and uses TCC's integrated assembler and
    linker; there is no external `as`/`ld` on Horus and none is needed.

    The in-process `-run` mode is NOT supported: it requires writable+
    executable (RWX) memory, which Horus's W^X policy forbids by design.
    Compile to a file and run that instead.

    Compiling a complete program on Horus additionally needs the C headers
    and library (and a C runtime) provisioned onto the filesystem under
    /usr/include and /usr/lib; that provisioning is a work in progress. Until
    it lands, `tcc -v`, option/usage output, and preprocessing/compilation of
    self-contained translation units to an object (`tcc -c`) work from the
    store.

EXIT STATUS
    0 on success, non-zero on error.

